 S~S  SimpleSal template documents: README information about working with SimpleSal source files

=====================

 S~S TruSoft Computing LLC (TSC LLC) Repository Philosophy

------------------------------------------

 S~S   SimpleSal explains the managed object concept

    This is the README about the managed objects in this repo.
    TSC LLC's idea of a managed object excludes anything present in the repo that is metadata.

    The repo database contains what TSC LLC calls the "repo object": that thing the repo controls.
        The repo database MANAGER applications maintain metadata about the repo object.

    A "managed object" is what TSC LLC calls everything in the repo, EXCEPT files ABOUT the repo.
        The repo database OWNER maintains metadata about the managed object.
        The repo database OWNER invents conventions to help separate managed object from METADATA.

    TSC LLC's chosen publishing style:
        1) the repo contains human metadata text files and the managed object as defined here;
        2) the conventions followed for separating the metadata is adopted from GITHUB and LINUX;
        3) the managed object is a single subdirectory in the root of the repository.

------------------------------------------

